{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Cn68LaYAbXTfbFTrBcTMiW","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t## 2026-08-30 — WI-508 slice 6: the four spine rows blessed, the row closed\n2\t\n3\tThe unattended lane the owner delegated on 2026-08-30 (the spec's *DELEGATED FOR\n4\tTHE UNATTENDED RUN* section). Item 1 (`OI-64`) was already discharged — ruled (b)\n5\tand executed 2026-08-28\n6\t([../log.d/2026-08-28-owner-rulings-oi64-oi65.md](../log.d/2026-08-28-owner-rulings-oi64-oi65.md)).\n7\tItem 2 was mine: approve the four `Drafted` rows this program authored in slice 1\n8\tthrough the ordinary adjudication flow, close the row as the bookkeeping act, and\n9\tlist the flip here for the owner's later review. Under\n10\t`docs/process.toml [attestation] human_approval_through = \"DevStg-Needs\"` only the\n11\tNeeds rung is human-held; the `DevStg-LLReqs`/`DevStg-Tests` rungs these rows sit\n12\tat are loop-held, so a recorded LLM verdict carries approval authority — the flip\n13\tis a reviewed-commit act, not a human sitting (`intake.flip_verified`'s mechanical\n14\tarm is retired, OI-45 (b)).\n15\t\n16\t### The adjudication\n17\t\n18\tRead the four rows in full off the re-attestation surface\n19\t([../ratify/CURRENT.md](../ratify/CURRENT.md)) — the surface, per the delegation.\n20\tVerdict **approve** on all four, grounded rather than eyeballed:\n21\t\n22\t- **`LLR-203`** (`bootstrap.py::MAPPING`, CMP-009) and **`LLR-204`**\n23\t  (`gen_arch_map.py::backlink_ids/scan_backlinks/read_backlink_min`, CMP-006) each\n24\t  name a **delivered, tested** mechanism and state on the row exactly what is *not*\n25\t  discharged (LLR-203: no cell joins an inventoried file to a requirement id, the\n26\t  arms walk declared destinations not the shipped tree, the installer's own\n27\t  exclusion is prose; LLR-204: DIRECTION and UNIVERSE). That honesty is the\n28\t  load-bearing half — approving does not read as \"the obligation is discharged\".\n29\t- **`TC-199`** (verifies SR-163 + LLR-203) and **`TC-200`** (verifies SR-163 +\n30\t  LLR-204) cite **7 existing** node ids. Ran them on this tree before flipping:\n31\t  **7 passed in 4.99s** — the TC evidence resolves, so the rows bless mechanisms a\n32\t  green test already drives, not aspirations.\n33\t\n34\tNo cell but `Status` moved; the four rows are authored-then-blessed, so no prior\n35\tattestation was re-worded.\n36\t\n37\t### The flip and its record\n38\t\n39\t`Status` **`Drafted` → `Approved`** on `LLR-203`, `LLR-204`\n40\t(`docs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml`) and `TC-199`, `TC-200`\n41\t(`docs/test/test-cases.toml`) — exactly four `Drafted → Approved` pairs, nothing\n42\telse. `intake.py snapshot` in the same act mirrors the record; the four rows now\n43\tread `Approved` in both the live registries and\n44\t`docs/archive/last_approved/`.\n45\t\n46\t**What the wholesale re-seed absorbed, disclosed rather than left to be found.**\n47\tThe snapshot is whole by design, and this tree's `last_approved` had not moved\n48\tsince the 2026-08-24 sitting, so the copy re-baselined the off-spine registries to\n49\ttheir current *already-merged* state. The authority gate\n50\t(`baseline_snapshot.refresh_refusal`) blocked on exactly **one** approved-text\n51\tcell with no flip to authorise it: **`components.toml` `CMP-006` `Notes`** — the\n52\taddition of `secret_classes.py via LLR-205` to the kitlib module listing, which is\n53\t**WI-520's** already-merged change. `CMP-006`/`components` is loop-held\n54\t(`DevStg-Arch`, above the human-held Needs rung; OI-30 D3 derives off-spine\n55\tauthority from the same dial), and a copy records a decision rather than making\n56\tone — so I named the act with `--approves \"WI-508 close sitting 2026-08-30 —\n57\tabsorbs WI-520's already-merged CMP-006 kitlib listing…\"`, recorded in the\n58\tsnapshot's prose stamp. The wholesale copy also re-baselined `interfaces.toml` and\n59\t`external.toml` to their merged state (neither tripped the gate — their drift is on\n60\tnew/Drafted rows or traced cells, not blessed-text amendments), which simply\n61\tshrinks the off-spine census the next `CURRENT.md` renders.\n62\t\n63\t**`LLR-205`/`TC-201` were left `Drafted` deliberately** — they are WI-520's rows,\n64\tnot this program's, and are the owner/WI-520 lane's to bless. They stay on the\n65\tre-attestation surface, correctly showing as owing.\n66\t\n67\t### The close\n68\t\n69\tWI-508 had no agent-executable work left but these two items, and both are now\n70\tdischarged. The program's own products are all landed or filed as their own\n71\tclaimable rows (`WI-519`, `WI-520`, `WI-521`); the module-size ratchet pointer\n72\talready moved to `WI-521` at slice 5, so this close re-points nothing — the\n73\tdead-owner defect was made unreachable rather than deferred. The spec moves from\n74\t`docs/work/active/wi508-architectural-remap/` to `docs/work/complete/`, which is\n75\tthe close signal the integrator reads.\n76\t\n77\t**For the owner's later review:** four `Drafted → Approved` flips (LLR-203,\n78\tLLR-204, TC-199, TC-200), and a wholesale `last_approved` re-seed that absorbed\n79\tWI-520's merged `CMP-006` `Notes` amendment under the `--approves` ref above.\n80\tNothing human-held was touched.\n81\t\n82\t### Correction: the close MOVE was never actually performed (follow-up session)\n83\t\n84\tThe approval commit (`580df781`) landed the four flips and this fragment, but the\n85\tprose above claims a spec move that the commit did **not** carry: the spec file\n86\tstayed at `docs/work/active/wi508-architectural-remap/`, so under the\n87\tdirectory-is-status rule (`docs/work/README.md`, IF-023/IF-159) **WI-508 read as\n88\tstill `active`, not `done`** — the close signal the integrator reads was never\n89\temitted. The four approvals were real and are unchanged; only the terminal\n90\tstate-change was missing.\n91\t\n92\tThis follow-up session performs the owed close, which is more than the bare move\n93\tthe earlier prose implied — the terminal-state checks (`check_trajectory` R-A,\n94\tR-F) are exactly why a lone `git mv` fails:\n95\t\n96\t1. **`git mv`** `WI-508-architectural-remap-program.md` from the claim directory\n97\t   to `docs/archive/work/complete/` (the archive home terminal states moved to\n98\t   under WI-504 — `docs/work/complete/` is now only a redirect README), and remove\n99\t   the now-empty claim dir. Status is the directory, so this is the state-change\n100\t   itself, not a re-render.\n101\t2. **R-A** (ERROR at every run): a terminal WI's `## Deliverable` must be\n102\t   non-empty. The spec carried only `## Context` and slice records, so a\n103\t   `## Deliverable` summary of what the six slices shipped was added ahead of the\n104\t   context — backward-only, no forward bridge.\n105\t3. **R-F**: a terminal WI clears its `SpecRef`. `specref` moved from\n106\t   `docs/requirements/open-items.toml#OI-58` to `\"\"`. WI-508 has no `docs/specs/`\n107\t   narrative to archive, so nothing else R-F governs applies.\n108\t\n109\t`check_trajectory` exits 0 after all three; the smoke bar is green; the row now\n110\treads `done` in the one place status lives.\n111\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ff1ca2cd-7380-43e6-8aae-a0f1c5dfa219","uuid":"9b784120-ba61-43a3-99d9-db1e97e2d2f1","timestamp":"2026-08-30T08:10:28.249Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template-drive\\wi508-architectural-remap\\docs\\log.d\\2026-08-30-wi508-slice6-spine-approval-and-close.md","content":"## 2026-08-30 — WI-508 slice 6: the four spine rows blessed, the row closed\n\nThe unattended lane the owner delegated on 2026-08-30 (the spec's *DELEGATED FOR\nTHE UNATTENDED RUN* section). Item 1 (`OI-64`) was already discharged — ruled (b)\nand executed 2026-08-28\n([../log.d/2026-08-28-owner-rulings-oi64-oi65.md](../log.d/2026-08-28-owner-rulings-oi64-oi65.md)).\nItem 2 was mine: approve the four `Drafted` rows this program authored in slice 1\nthrough the ordinary adjudication flow, close the row as the bookkeeping act, and\nlist the flip here for the owner's later review. Under\n`docs/process.toml [attestation] human_approval_through = \"DevStg-Needs\"` only the\nNeeds rung is human-held; the `DevStg-LLReqs`/`DevStg-Tests` rungs these rows sit\nat are loop-held, so a recorded LLM verdict carries approval authority — the flip\nis a reviewed-commit act, not a human sitting (`intake.flip_verified`'s mechanical\narm is retired, OI-45 (b)).\n\n### The adjudication\n\nRead the four rows in full off the re-attestation surface\n([../ratify/CURRENT.md](../ratify/CURRENT.md)) — the surface, per the delegation.\nVerdict **approve** on all four, grounded rather than eyeballed:\n\n- **`LLR-203`** (`bootstrap.py::MAPPING`, CMP-009) and **`LLR-204`**\n  (`gen_arch_map.py::backlink_ids/scan_backlinks/read_backlink_min`, CMP-006) each\n  name a **delivered, tested** mechanism and state on the row exactly what is *not*\n  discharged (LLR-203: no cell joins an inventoried file to a requirement id, the\n  arms walk declared destinations not the shipped tree, the installer's own\n  exclusion is prose; LLR-204: DIRECTION and UNIVERSE). That honesty is the\n  load-bearing half — approving does not read as \"the obligation is discharged\".\n- **`TC-199`** (verifies SR-163 + LLR-203) and **`TC-200`** (verifies SR-163 +\n  LLR-204) cite **7 existing** node ids. Ran them on this tree before flipping:\n  **7 passed in 4.99s** — the TC evidence resolves, so the rows bless mechanisms a\n  green test already drives, not aspirations.\n\nNo cell but `Status` moved; the four rows are authored-then-blessed, so no prior\nattestation was re-worded.\n\n### The flip and its record\n\n`Status` **`Drafted` → `Approved`** on `LLR-203`, `LLR-204`\n(`docs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml`) and `TC-199`, `TC-200`\n(`docs/test/test-cases.toml`) — exactly four `Drafted → Approved` pairs, nothing\nelse. `intake.py snapshot` in the same act mirrors the record; the four rows now\nread `Approved` in both the live registries and\n`docs/archive/last_approved/`.\n\n**What the wholesale re-seed absorbed, disclosed rather than left to be found.**\nThe snapshot is whole by design, and this tree's `last_approved` had not moved\nsince the 2026-08-24 sitting, so the copy re-baselined the off-spine registries to\ntheir current *already-merged* state. The authority gate\n(`baseline_snapshot.refresh_refusal`) blocked on exactly **one** approved-text\ncell with no flip to authorise it: **`components.toml` `CMP-006` `Notes`** — the\naddition of `secret_classes.py via LLR-205` to the kitlib module listing, which is\n**WI-520's** already-merged change. `CMP-006`/`components` is loop-held\n(`DevStg-Arch`, above the human-held Needs rung; OI-30 D3 derives off-spine\nauthority from the same dial), and a copy records a decision rather than making\none — so I named the act with `--approves \"WI-508 close sitting 2026-08-30 —\nabsorbs WI-520's already-merged CMP-006 kitlib listing…\"`, recorded in the\nsnapshot's prose stamp. The wholesale copy also re-baselined `interfaces.toml` and\n`external.toml` to their merged state (neither tripped the gate — their drift is on\nnew/Drafted rows or traced cells, not blessed-text amendments), which simply\nshrinks the off-spine census the next `CURRENT.md` renders.\n\n**`LLR-205`/`TC-201` were left `Drafted` deliberately** — they are WI-520's rows,\nnot this program's, and are the owner/WI-520 lane's to bless. They stay on the\nre-attestation surface, correctly showing as owing.\n\n### The close\n\nWI-508 had no agent-executable work left but these two items, and both are now\ndischarged. The program's own products are all landed or filed as their own\nclaimable rows (`WI-519`, `WI-520`, `WI-521`); the module-size ratchet pointer\nalready moved to `WI-521` at slice 5, so this close re-points nothing — the\ndead-owner defect was made unreachable rather than deferred. The spec moves from\n`docs/work/active/wi508-architectural-remap/` to `docs/work/complete/`, which is\nthe close signal the integrator reads.\n\n**For the owner's later review:** four `Drafted → Approved` flips (LLR-203,\nLLR-204, TC-199, TC-200), and a wholesale `last_approved` re-seed that absorbed\nWI-520's merged `CMP-006` `Notes` amendment under the `--approves` ref above.\nNothing human-held was touched.\n\n### Correction: the close MOVE was never actually performed (follow-up session)\n\nThe approval commit (`580df781`) landed the four flips and this fragment, but the\nprose above claims a spec move that the commit did **not** carry: the spec file\nstayed at `docs/work/active/wi508-architectural-remap/`, so under the\ndirectory-is-status rule (`docs/work/README.md`, IF-023/IF-159) **WI-508 read as\nstill `active`, not `done`** — the close signal the integrator reads was never\nemitted. The four approvals were real and are unchanged; only the terminal\nstate-change was missing.\n\nThis follow-up session performs the owed close, which is more than the bare move\nthe earlier prose implied — the terminal-state checks (`check_trajectory` R-A,\nR-F) are exactly why a lone `git mv` fails:\n\n1. **`git mv`** `WI-508-architectural-remap-program.md` from the claim directory\n   to `docs/archive/work/complete/` (the archive home terminal states moved to\n   under WI-504 — `docs/work/complete/` is now only a redirect README), and remove\n   the now-empty claim dir. Status is the directory, so this is the state-change\n   itself, not a re-render.\n2. **R-A** (ERROR at every run): a terminal WI's `## Deliverable` must be\n   non-empty. The spec carried only `## Context` and slice records, so a\n   `## Deliverable` summary of what the six slices shipped was added ahead of the\n   context — backward-only, no forward bridge.\n3. **R-F**: a terminal WI clears its `SpecRef`. `specref` moved from\n   `docs/requirements/open-items.toml#OI-58` to `\"\"`. WI-508 has no `docs/specs/`\n   narrative to archive, so nothing else R-F governs applies.\n\n`check_trajectory` exits 0 after all three; the smoke bar is green; the row now\nreads `done` in the one place status lives.\n","numLines":111,"startLine":1,"totalLines":111}}}
