{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TCVqCm413NymuEXFHZGXGv","type":"tool_result","content":"1995\tlevel = \"Unit\"\n1996\tmethod = \"\"\"Two claims, because the row makes two. THE RULES, each driven directly rather than through the engine: the orphan pass emits SR then LLR then TC then SN and returns exactly the at-fault ids of the findings it emitted; a Drafted SR stands the child-completeness rules down while its SN linkage still applies; a PB Refs cell resolves against an LLR Module path as well as against ids, and an empty one is a finding; a Component tag naming no CMP row is a finding while an empty component registry disarms the membership half entirely; a knowledge ref resolves only under the docs/knowledge prefix and a traversal ref never escapes the pack root; the phase scope covers the foundation phase under every filter and a blank Phase always; and the status criterion defers an out-of-phase row rather than failing it. THE BOUNDARY AND THE BAGS: assert that this module imports no sibling of the scripts directory, that the engine still answers to every moved name and that each definition lives here; that the loaded registry record is frozen, total, and constructed at exactly one site; that the findings record's list defaults are per instance and that the two fields filled after the pure pass returns are DECLARED rather than conjured at a call site; that the flags record accepts either itself or a CLI namespace; that no caller imports argparse to forge the engine's config; and that the composer stays a composer - measured line span, and no nested def, which is how the number this split removed got to fifty.\"\"\"\n1997\ttier = \"Smoke\"\n1998\texpected = \"Satisfies the acceptance folded into LLR-201 (parent SR-157)\"\n1999\tautomated = \"Yes\"\n2000\tevidence = \"\"\"tests/test_trace_coherence.py::test_the_orphan_rules_emit_sr_then_llr_then_tc_then_sn; tests/test_trace_coherence.py::test_a_drafted_row_stands_the_child_rules_down_but_not_its_sn_link; tests/test_trace_coherence.py::test_off_spine_backlinks_resolve_against_ids_and_llr_module_paths; tests/test_trace_coherence.py::test_component_membership_is_checked_from_the_primitive_side; tests/test_trace_coherence.py::test_the_knowledge_ref_resolves_only_the_pack_prefix; tests/test_trace_coherence.py::test_the_phase_scope_always_covers_the_foundation_phase; tests/test_trace_coherence.py::test_the_status_criterion_defers_out_of_phase_and_stands_down_for_drafted; tests/test_trace_coherence.py::test_registries_is_frozen_and_total; tests/test_trace_coherence.py::test_the_loader_is_the_only_construction_site_of_registries; tests/test_trace_coherence.py::test_findings_list_defaults_are_per_instance; tests/test_trace_coherence.py::test_the_two_post_analyze_fields_are_declared_not_conjured; tests/test_trace_coherence.py::test_analysis_flags_takes_a_record_or_a_namespace; tests/test_trace_coherence.py::test_no_caller_forges_an_argparse_namespace_for_the_engine; tests/test_trace_coherence.py::test_the_coherence_rules_import_no_sibling_of_scripts; tests/test_trace_coherence.py::test_trace_re_exports_every_moved_name; tests/test_trace_coherence.py::test_analyze_is_a_composer_and_stays_one\"\"\"\n2001\tstatus = \"Approved\"\n2002\tphase = 5\n2003\t[test.TC-198]\n2004\tverifies = [\"SR-161\", \"LLR-202\"]\n2005\tlevel = \"Unit\"\n2006\tmethod = \"\"\"Drive the arm over a real two-commit git repository whose HEAD holds an Approved SR-001 (and, for the tier case, an Approved LLR-001 and TC-001), with the change STAGED rather than committed - the hook's own question. FIRES: the requirement cell amended while Hat-Refs stands raises one finding naming the row and the moved cells, with the amendment arm firing alongside it so the second arm is proven an addition rather than a re-spelling. SILENT ON TRACED-ONLY MOVEMENT: writing the Hat-Refs cell itself - the perspective backfill's own edit - raises nothing, and neither does an SN-Refs re-point. SILENT WHEN DISCHARGED: substance and Hat-Refs moving together raises nothing here while the amendment arm still fires. VACUOUS WHERE THERE IS NO BASELINE, both shapes: a row minted in the staged commit, and a row amended below approval on both sides. STRUCTURALLY SILENT ON A TIER WITH NO SUCH COLUMN: an LLR and a TC amended in the same commit yield exactly one finding, the LLR's, so the scoping cannot pass by the arm being silent everywhere.\"\"\"\n2007\ttier = \"Smoke\"\n2008\texpected = \"Satisfies the acceptance folded into LLR-202 (parent SR-161)\"\n2009\tautomated = \"Yes\"\n2010\tevidence = \"\"\"tests/test_trajectory_staged.py::test_amending_approved_cells_without_moving_hat_refs_warns; tests/test_trajectory_staged.py::test_hat_refs_arm_is_silent_when_only_traced_cells_move; tests/test_trajectory_staged.py::test_hat_refs_arm_is_silent_when_the_cell_moves_with_the_amendment; tests/test_trajectory_staged.py::test_hat_refs_arm_is_vacuous_where_a_row_has_no_baseline; tests/test_trajectory_staged.py::test_hat_refs_arm_is_silent_on_a_tier_that_carries_no_such_column\"\"\"\n2011\tstatus = \"Approved\"\n2012\tphase = 5\n2013\t\n2014\t[test.TC-199]\n2015\tverifies = [\"SR-163\", \"LLR-203\"]\n2016\tlevel = \"Integration\"\n2017\tmethod = \"\"\"The inventory's two delivered finding classes, driven where each one can actually fail. THE DOGFOOD DIRECTION, in process against the live MAPPING literal: a declared destination that this repository neither carries nor serves in place out of the kit tree, and which no absence declaration covers, is reported by name; a declared absence whose destination has materialized is reported as stale, with the lifecycle marker exempting only the paths whose presence is a legal state; and the walk is bite-proofed by removing one declared entry and asserting its destination reappears in the finding set, so a walk that had quietly stopped looking could not pass. THE PACKAGE DIRECTION, asked of a REAL bootstrapped scaffold rather than of the kit tree, because the kit's own scripts directory holds every file and a partial copy reads green there: the copied helper package must hold exactly the kit's module set - a missing or stale MAPPING row is named as the cause - and must import from where a shipped script sits; and a shipped script importing a sibling the inventory omits is reported against the MAPPING literal read as an AST, never as a whole-file regex, so a comment naming a module cannot mark it mapped.\"\"\"\n2018\ttier = \"Full\"\n2019\texpected = \"Satisfies the acceptance folded into LLR-203 (parent SR-163)\"\n2020\tautomated = \"Yes\"\n2021\tevidence = \"\"\"tests/test_dogfood_sync.py::test_scaffold_mapping_covered_or_declared; tests/test_dogfood_sync.py::test_scaffold_omissions_list_is_current; tests/test_dogfood_sync.py::test_bite_scaffold_walk_catches_an_undeclared_absence; tests/test_bootstrap.py::test_the_common_package_ships_complete; tests/test_bootstrap.py::test_every_sibling_imported_module_is_shipped_by_mapping\"\"\"\n2022\tstatus = \"Approved\"\n2023\tphase = 5\n2024\t\n2025\t[test.TC-200]\n2026\tverifies = [\"SR-163\", \"LLR-204\"]\n2027\tlevel = \"Integration\"\n2028\tmethod = \"\"\"The grammar and the policy, separately, because they fail separately. THE GRAMMAR, driven directly on the shared function both the map column and the coverage percentage read, so a divergence between the two is unrepresentable: a declaration token opening a line yields its spine ids; prose naming ids without the token yields none; a token PRECEDED by prose yields none, including the two shapes that had previously harvested a sentence denying a link as a declaration of it; whitespace, comment markers and quote characters may precede the token and nothing else may; a wrapped list continuation line declares nothing. THE POLICY, driven through the real command line on a real bootstrapped scaffold rather than by reading the code: with a threshold declared in the policy home and a live design row that no source declaration names, the report prints the shortfall and exits ZERO, and only the explicit strict arm turns the same reading into a nonzero exit - which is what makes the threshold a gate a repository opts into rather than one the delivered package arms on its behalf.\"\"\"\n2029\ttier = \"Full\"\n2030\texpected = \"Satisfies the acceptance folded into LLR-204 (parent SR-163)\"\n2031\tautomated = \"Yes\"\n2032\tevidence = \"\"\"tests/test_gen_arch_map.py::test_backlink_ids_is_the_one_definition_of_a_declaration; tests/test_gen_arch_map.py::test_backlink_cli_is_warn_first_and_strict_only_on_demand\"\"\"\n2033\tstatus = \"Approved\"\n2034\tphase = 5\n2035\t\n2036\t[test.TC-201]\n2037\tverifies = [\"SR-017\", \"SR-176\", \"LLR-205\"]\n2038\tlevel = \"Integration\"\n2039\tmethod = \"\"\"Drives check_privacy.py's Scanner (secrets floor) and agent_common.py's redact_secrets against a shared sample set, three ways. FIRST, a five-sample driven table: a PEM private-key block now catches on both sides (was floor-catch/redactor-miss); a Bearer token, a short GitHub token and a short API key stay floor-miss/redactor-catch, the three DELIBERATE threshold asymmetries kitlib.secret_classes.SECRET_CLASSES states p
